---

<DocsLayout
  title="Audience profiles & stats"
  description="Manage ilyStream audience profiles, primary accounts, merged identities, platform badges, status filters, and engagement stats."
  slug="audience-stats"
  updated="July 2026"
  readingTime="10 min"
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
  <p>
    Audience Stats turns separate TikTok, Twitch, YouTube, and Kick accounts into
    readable ilyStream profiles. It tracks lifetime engagement, platform accounts,
    badges, AI usage, songs, chats, gifts, likes, shares, raids, revenue, and last
    seen time.
  </p>

  <h2 id="primary">Primary accounts</h2>
  <p>
    A primary account controls which display name and avatar the ilyStream profile
    should use. This is useful when one viewer has an old alt, a display-name-only
    entry, or multiple TikTok accounts connected.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Open Audience Stats.</strong> Click a user row to expand their profile.</li>
    <li><strong>Find the account they are best known by.</strong> Use the account cards under the expanded profile.</li>
    <li><strong>Click Use picture or Primary.</strong> The profile display name and avatar should update to match that one account only.</li>
    <li><strong>Verify platform scope.</strong> Setting one TikTok account as primary should not mark every TikTok alt as primary.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="merge">Merge bad identities</h2>
  <p>
    Older builds could accidentally treat display names as usernames. Merge those
    records into the real account instead of keeping duplicate rows.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Open the incorrect profile.</strong> Example: a display-name account that does not exist as a real handle.</li>
    <li><strong>Find the real account card.</strong> Look for the real username or linked platform account.</li>
    <li><strong>Use the merge or link action.</strong> Move the stats into the correct ilyStream profile.</li>
    <li><strong>Set the primary afterward.</strong> Pick the real account as primary so the avatar and name stay correct.</li>
    <li><strong>Refresh Audience Stats.</strong> Confirm the duplicate no longer appears as a separate top user.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="badges">Badge order</h2>
  <p>
    Badges and platform icons follow a stable order so the table is readable even
    when users have different combinations.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Platform icons</strong>: TikTok, Twitch, YouTube, Kick.</li>
    <li><strong>Moderator badges first</strong>: TikTok mod, Twitch mod, YouTube mod, Kick mod.</li>
    <li><strong>Other badges after mods</strong>: TikTok fan club, TikTok super fan, Twitch subscriber, YouTube superfan, Kick supporter badges.</li>
    <li><strong>Platform-specific badges stay scoped</strong>: selecting Twitch Subscribers should show Twitch subscriber accounts, not TikTok fan club accounts.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="sorting">Sorting and filters</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Use platform filter.</strong> Choose all platforms or one service.</li>
    <li><strong>Use Sort by.</strong> Sort by overall rank, likes, gifts, revenue, shares, raids, chats, songs, or AI usage.</li>
    <li><strong>Use Status.</strong> Filter by moderators, subscribers, superfans, or <em>None</em> when you want to stop badge-specific sorting.</li>
    <li><strong>Click rows to expand.</strong> Expanded rows show account cards and per-account stats.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="stats">Stats columns</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Overall</strong>: the user rank across all tracked categories.</li>
    <li><strong>Likes, gifts, revenue, shares, raids, chats, songs</strong>: lifetime counters across linked accounts.</li>
    <li><strong>AI</strong>: counted when a viewer intentionally invokes the AI command path.</li>
    <li><strong>Last seen</strong>: newest event time from any linked account.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</h2>
  <p><strong>A placeholder avatar appears.</strong> Expand the profile, choose the account with the correct avatar, and set it as primary.</p>
  <p><strong>All alts become primary.</strong> That is wrong behavior. Primary selection should attach to one account id, not every account on the same platform.</p>
  <p><strong>Mod badges are missing.</strong> Reconnect the platform and wait for fresh chat events; mod status often arrives with message metadata.</p>
  <p><strong>A fake username exists.</strong> Merge the fake display-name record into the real handle, then set the real handle as primary.</p>

